  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NextGen4EU: Youth Fellowship Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project significantly increases the capacity of Ukrainian institutions by forming a new generation of specialists capable of professionally supporting the process of Ukraine&#x2019;s accession to the EU in the medium and long term. European integration is not only a political decision, but also an intensive technical, legal and administrative process that requires significant human resources, in particular young analysts, lawyers, economists and managers. Today, state bodies are experiencing a shortage of such personnel.

By creating a structured pipeline for training young people, the project strengthens the institutional capacity of the state: participants gain knowledge about EU institutions, policies, enlargement procedures, negotiation clusters and real requirements for adapting legislation. The combination of training, mentoring and practical graduation projects ensures not only academic but also operational readiness of future specialists.

A key mechanism for increasing capacity is internships in government bodies, where young specialists work with real tasks, contribute to the analysis of the acquis, the preparation of positions, internal coordination and policy development. This creates a rapid human resource pool for European integration, and also brings additional expertise to state institutions already during the project implementation.

The project also reduces regional inequality by opening up opportunities for participants from all regions, contributes to the growth of youth trust in the civil service, and forms the NextGen4EU community - the future pillar of Ukraine in negotiations with the EU. Thus, it strengthens the human, institutional and societal capacity necessary for Ukraine&apos;s successful and sustainable movement towards membership in the European Union.</narrative>
  </description>
